    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"font-family:'gg sans', 'Noto Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Symbols'\">Every year, as the long winters of the north end, stories of the cold months would find their way to the cities from those that live in the countryside. Many stories claim that the howls on the wind during blizzards were often accompanied by a feeling of being watched by something just out of view. Stories of Fah’rin tell of a massive wolf-like deity that seeks to halt the world; burying it beneath layers of snow and ice, perfectly preserved, perfectly still. Followers of Fah’rin can often be seen carrying her unholy symbol, a wolven face with an open maw, its fangs made of ice.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'gg sans', 'Noto Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Symbols'\"><strong>Edicts</strong> sculpt ice into vicious shapes, do not fear the cold, perfect yourself</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'gg sans', 'Noto Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Symbols'\"><strong>Anathema</strong> create fires for warmth, intentionally melt ice, harm a wolf that has done you no wrong</span></p>"
